+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Generate cases/full-chain: a five-stage intrusion across two workstations and the DC.
+
+The fifth case, and the largest -- a >10 MB JSON-lines estate. It chains four public
+EVTX-ATTACK-SAMPLES recordings into one continuous story, re-seeds every identifier, and
+buries the chain in a much larger synthetic estate (>24k events across six workstations,
+a management server and a domain controller):
+
+  Execution (encoded PowerShell foothold)                    4688 / Sysmon 1  powershell -Enc
+  Credential Access/sysmon_10_..._logonpasswords.evtx        Sysmon 10  lsass access 0x1010
+  Lateral Movement/LM_WMI_4624_4688_TargetHost.evtx          4624 type-3, 4688 WmiPrvSE->cmd
+  Lateral Movement/LM_ScheduledTask_ATSVC_target_host.evtx   4698 task registered
+  Credential Access/CA_DCSync_4662.evtx                      4662 DS replication (DCSync)
+
+The story (all identifiers re-seeded, nothing matches a memorised sample):
+
+  1. FOOTHOLD (WKS-A). A phished user opens a document; OUTLOOK.EXE spawns
+     powershell.exe -Enc <b64> -- an encoded PowerShell command that beacons out.
+  2. CREDENTIAL ACCESS (WKS-A). The foothold dumps LSASS: cmd -> rundll32
+     comsvcs.dll,MiniDump, and a process reads lsass.exe with GrantedAccess 0x1010.
+     From that dump the attacker recovers a privileged account, `svc_backup`.
+  3. LATERAL MOVEMENT (WKS-A -> WKS-B). Using svc_backup, a type-3 logon to WKS-B from
+     WKS-A's IP, then WmiPrvSE.exe (WMI, SYSTEM) spawns cmd.exe. THIS is the tip the
+     alert fires on -- the middle of the chain.
+  4. PERSISTENCE (WKS-B). The WMI cmd registers a scheduled task (4698) whose action is a
+     SECOND encoded PowerShell payload; ~50 minutes later the task fires under SYSTEM with
+     no logon behind it, running the same base64.
+  5. DOMAIN DOMINANCE (WKS-B -> DC). svc_backup logs on to the DC (type-3, from WKS-B's
+     IP) and performs a DCSync: Event 4662 against the directory with AccessMask 0x100 and
+     the DS-Replication-Get-Changes control-access GUID {1131f6aa-9c07-11d1-f79f-...} --
+     a replication request from a workstation account, not a DC.
+
+The alert fires only on the shallow tip of stage 3 -- "cmd.exe spawned by WmiPrvSE.exe on
+WKS-B" -- exactly the wmi-lsass signature, and (as there) benign WMI activity is everywhere.
+The investigation has to extend that one line in BOTH directions: back through the LSASS
+dump and the encoded foothold on WKS-A that produced svc_backup, and forward through the
+scheduled task and the DCSync that svc_backup then drove against the DC. The join across
+all five stages is the account `svc_backup` and the per-hop source IPs; stage 4 has its own
+join (the same base64 in the task action and the fired command line).
+
+The join tokens: the stolen account name, the per-hop logon ids, and the two base64
+payloads. Logs are JSON lines; keys are ordered so ts/event_id/computer lead and the long
+discriminators (CommandLine, TaskContent, GrantedAccess, Properties) trail.
+
+Usage:
+    python3 scripts/make_full_chain_case.py [--out cases/full-chain]
+                                            [--evtx-dir cases/_evtx] [--target-mb 11]
+GROUND_TRUTH.md is written to the case root, NOT into logs/, so analyze.py never reads it.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import json
+import random
+import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
+from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
+from pathlib import Path
+
+SEED = 20260909
+
+# -- the estate ------------------------------------------------------------------------
+DOMAIN = "CORP"
+
+# Stage 1-2: the foothold + credential-theft host.
+HOST_A = "WKS-5581"
+IP_A = "10.12.34.81"
+MAC_A = "00:1b:44:11:80:1a"
+# The phished user whose interactive session launches the encoded PowerShell.
+FOOTHOLD_USER = "r.delgado"
+FOOTHOLD_SID = "S-1-5-21-341049218-2894104772-1560093651-1157"
